```

If we can assume that the compiler can optimize it so that

```c
if (foo) {
   bar();
}

if (foo && zoo) {
   zar();
}
```

Generates the same binary as 

```c
if (foo) {
    bar();
    
    if (zoo) {
        zar();
    }
}
```

Then I'm absolutely fine with it :) If `foo` needs to be evaluated twice for the sake of readability, then we are effectively saying that performance is less important than readability, which can be a slippery slope in some cases :)
